  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2006-11-24T04:41:56-06:00",
   "body": "Its quite hard to kill them at lvl 14 or lower, i tried it and died three times at 13 in moonbrook.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2007-01-08T02:05:38-06:00",
   "body": "I did this quest in a group with me (lvl 16 human warrior) and a lvl 15 human warlock. The warlock's pet took most of the damage and we were able to do it in about half an hour.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2004-09-13T00:00:56-05:00",
   "body": "The pillagers can be found at a small camp west of Sentinal Hill, or in Gold Coast Quarry cave.",
   "replies": [
    "Also at the Alexston Farmstead, roundabout 38,56.\n\n_________\nSylarlis\n33 Night Elf Rogue\nKul Tiras\nDefenders of Honor"
   ]
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2005-02-10T23:56:01-06:00",
   "body": "they are also found in the moonglow city (or something like that).  however, they are higher level  here, and harder to see.  i like the coastal camp area better that qamgine mentioned.",
   "replies": [
    "Moonbrook 43,66"
   ]
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2019-11-20T02:24:35-06:00",
   "body": "Pro Tip for melee: Farm these in Moonbrook. Looters generally aren't a problem, but they will use Backstab if you turn your back to them; it's fast and hits hard. However, the Pillagers tend to give melee a lot of trouble due to the Frost Armor's attack speed slow. LoS them on the buildings and walls, and then it becomes massively easy to take on 2-3 at once to keep interrupting their brutal Fireballs and getting free damage.",
   "replies": []
  },
